Z||000000||ur2biteme||08-06-2000||06:12 AM||||does anyone make split c.v. boots for the inner boot?  i've got an '87 4cly 5speed and i don't wanna have to pull the axle.  i don't want to have to replace it either, other than spraying grease out, it works perfectly.  it's also a bit of a cost issue as well.  please let me know.  <P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||rprevo||08-06-2000||09:59 AM|||| There is a splitboot, It's a one size fit's<BR>all, It's made by motormite and the product<BR>is called SPEEDI-BOOT. They work<BR>allright but you have to take your time<BR>with installing it. <P>Ray||||reg||6
Z||000002||GT Bastard||08-06-2000||02:00 PM||||I can pull both my axles in under 10 minutes now. It's not hard at all!  Then again, that's with air tools.  hehehe...||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||08-06-2000||02:04 PM||||If the only problem is spraying grease, then the split boots should work well to replace solid ones, as the split boots will maintain the grease splattering. I would never consider using a split boot.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-06-2000||04:06 PM||||split boots will work well Only if they are installed very carefully. You absolutly must keep the mating surfaces clean and glue them exactly the way the instructions indicate or they will not hold up long.<P>Motormite very likely does make one for the Fiero inner. They make a bunch of them to cover nearly every CV made. You may have to have it ordered. You may have to spend time digging in the Motormite "master catalog" to find it. Motormite is like the Sears of odd little car things.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ur2biteme||08-08-2000||07:05 AM||||thanks for the help guys.  yeah, right now i think i used some super glue and duct tape to patch it for the time being and i hate not doing something right, but on the other hand, i really don't have the facilities or money at my disposal to fix it the way i would like.  not like i like the idea of the split boot either, but if i can get out cheap here, make it last a little over a year, then i can replace all this stuff when i go to swap the engine.  This car needs suspension stuff BAD.<P>anyway, ogre, i take little stock in what kragen says usually (no flames please from anyone who may work there) but they said that they didn't make one for the inner.  where would i go about looking for the catalog?  like NAPA or something?  <P>thanks again||||reg||1
